topic    keys
summary  the keys of the line editor
---
  Left Right, Ctrl-B Ctrl-F    move by a character
  Home End, Ctrl-A Ctrl-E      to the start or the end
  Backspace Delete             erase a character
  Ctrl-W                       erase the word before the cursor
  Ctrl-U Ctrl-K                erase to the start, or to the end
  Up Down                      the lines you ran that start with what is typed
  Ctrl-R                       search the lines you ran; Enter takes the one shown
  Tab                          complete a command, a file name or an option
  Right at the end             take the suggestion shown in faint text
  Ctrl-L                       clear the screen
  Ctrl-C                       drop the line
  Enter                        run the line; with a quote or { open, continue it on the next
  Ctrl-D                       nothing: type exit to end the shell

